# Starforge Subscriptions — modular ownership

Any Starforge feature that sells **recurring access** (player premium, organizer premium, advertisements) **must** use `product:subscriptions`. Payments only charges and snapshots. Do not ship a second plan catalog, period table, or entitlement store inside Events, Ads, Marketplace, or Payments.

## Source of truth

| Concern | Owner |
| --- | --- |
| Plan catalog, periods, trial/renew/upgrade rules, entitlement keys, seats | **`product:subscriptions`** — `@/modules/subscriptions/api` |
| Charge, VAT, coupons, gateways, invoices, refunds, recurring intents | **`product:payments`** |
| Lifecycle / reminder mail | **`product:email-manager`** — `emitEmailTrigger` / starters |
| Optional signup field schema | **`product:forms`** — definition + `subscription-registration` preset |
| User groups + ACL permission matrix | **Core ACL** — Subscriptions may only **add/remove members** for plan `groupIds` |
| Member / group ticket amounts | **`product:events`** — asks `resolveAudience` / `hasEntitlement` |
| Ad placement / listing rank | **`product:ads`** / Marketplace (later) — asks `hasEntitlement` |
| Merchant collect boolean stub | Payments `sf_pay_collect_entitlements` (frozen) → replaced by `payments.collect` when Subscriptions is on |

## Access model (hybrid)

| Surface | Mechanism |
| --- | --- |
| Pages, nav, admin areas, later NetSuite chrome | Core **groups** — plan `groupIds` synced to `sf_user_group_members` while period active |
| Domain logic (ticket price, `payments.collect`, `events.manage`) | **`hasEntitlement` / `resolveAudience`** — period windows + grace |

On activate: `addUserToGroup` for each plan/period group. On expire/refund: remove a group only if no other active period still lists it. Never write `sf_acl_permissions` from this pack. Deep-link group/ACL admin to `/admin/users`.

## Subjects

Type is `subject`. Subtype is `audience` (no second column). Blank player / organizer audiences are the original premiums.

- `membership` — players. Subtypes: `premium` (blank counts as this), `premium_plus`
- `organizer` — organizers. Subtypes: `organizer` (blank counts as this), `brand` (a brand that owns a managed page — a site page that operates as their website)
- `advertisement` — subtypes: `organizer`, `marketplace`, `brand`, `shop`
- `other` — catch-all. Unknown subject strings filter here

Subject and audience are open strings. Do not add a new subscription module for a new kind.

## Lifecycle (Subscriptions owns rules; Payments owns money)

- **Free plans** — activate locally (no cart).
- **Paid / charged trial** — Payments checkout; hook `subscriptions.activate`.
- **Manual renew** — same plan checkout; extends `endsAt`.
- **Upgrade** — target must be in plan `upgradeTargetIds`; one active period per subject; proration credit calculated here, charged via Payments.
- **Cancel at period end** — flips flag; cancels Payments recurring id when present.
- **Auto-renew** — plan `recurringSupported` + Payments `createRecurring`; this pack only stores the foreign key and grants on paid hooks.
- **Seats** — `sf_sub_seats` on parent period; seat members inherit entitlements via `resolveAudience`.

## Do

- Call `@/modules/subscriptions/api` for resolve and checkout start.
- Re-resolve plan price server-side at checkout (`resolveCheckoutPriceMajor`).
- Pass organizer access via live `hasEntitlement('events.manage')` on the `admin.events` gate — do not write ACL **permission** rows.
- Sync plan `groupIds` via Core `addUserToGroup` / `removeUserFromGroup` only.
- Emit `product:subscriptions/*` email triggers only; put `buyerEmail` on the payload; seed starters under Settings.
- Deep-link coupons → `/admin/payments/coupons`, mail → `/admin/email`, forms → `/admin/forms/[id]`, groups → `/admin/users`.

## Don’t

- Grow `sf_pay_collect_entitlements` into plans or periods.
- Put ASN currency / token ledger here.
- Build ad inventory or listing ranking inside this pack.
- Call `getMailer()` from Subscriptions.
- Host checkout UI, gateway settings, invoice series, or coupon tables here.
- Invent a second ACL matrix or Users/ACL UI inside Subscriptions.
